4. HOW TO ASK FOR PERMISSION

Open an issue at github.com/gmax29/Evoly-Info/issues or contact gmax29 on GitHub.
Please say who you are, which part of Evoly you want to use, and for what purpose.

A permission only counts if:
- it is given in writing (an answer on GitHub or by e-mail is enough),
- it comes from the owner himself, and
- it names you and your purpose.

A permission applies only to the person, the purpose and the scope it names. It cannot be passed
on to anyone else. Unless it says otherwise, the owner can withdraw it at any time for the future.
No answer means no. Silence is never permission.


